 "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/ops/analyst.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/ops/report_writer/editor.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/ops/report_writer/write.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/ops/report_writer/writer_contract.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/ops/report_writer/writer_kind.py", "packages/evals/tests/report_writer_support.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_analyst_skill_exports.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_report_writer_exports.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_report_writer_kind.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_report_writer_skill_version.py"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-skills-under-test.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "Test evidence is stale: no recorded run covers HEAD", "recommendation": "prawduct-hook test-status reports 'stale: no .test-evidence.json on disk'. Run the evals suite on the testament pool (and the integration suite before merging into report-kit/analyst) and record the evidence, so that chunk 01's 'default write is unchanged (replay tests green)' is shown rather than assumed. Scope: instance.", "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "warning", "title": "Objective measures cover 2 of the 5 bounce kinds; the plan asks for 'bounces by kind'", "recommendation": "The plan's Architecture lists 'bounces by kind' among the kind's objective measures. The analyst records five kinds (unparsed, shape, validity, invariant, max_tokens; ops/report_writer/analyst.py:141, tally.record_bounce). _measures (writer_kind.py:547-552) and WRITER_KIND_MEASURES (writer_contract.py:115-118) land only validity and invariant. Failure scenario: a skill edit that breaks submission format (more unparsed or shape bounces, which is the likeliest regression from editing skill text) or causes output-cap truncation (max_tokens) moves no measure. The gate then cannot see it unless the run also ends refused. Either add a measure for each recorded kind, derived from the analyst's Literal so a new kind cannot be missed, or record in the plan that the other three are descoped and why. Scope: instance.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/ops/report_writer/writer_kind.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/ops/report_writer/writer_contract.py"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "ReportWriterKind's failure classification and most of its refusal branches have no test", "recommendation": "test_report_writer_kind.py covers the happy path, the skill-not-given refusal and the withheld-note-lacking exclusion. The following have no test. (1) _failed (writer_kind.py:474-514): the account / provider / candidate split decides whether a provider outage or an account refusal excludes the cell as infra or counts against the arm as a candidate error. Misrouting it biases an A/B comparison, and nothing would catch a swapped branch. (2) prepare's model-name mismatch refusal (343-347), the factory-ValueError refusal (339-342) and the dollar-budget pricing refusal (348-349). (3) prepare's subject check (331-338): the one subject test is refused earlier by the engine's LeverCoordinateError, so the kind's own branch, including the 'no skill' case, never runs. (4) _case_input's missing-case, unreadable-case and unreadable-snapshot exclusions (405-429). Add one test per branch, at minimum (1) with a describer for each owner, driven through execute_run as the existing tests are. Scope: class, bounded to the branches of ReportWriterKind.prepare, _case_input and _failed.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/ops/report_writer/writer_kind.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_report_writer_kind.py"], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "writer_cell_timeout_s, the answer to chunk 02 step 0, is untested and nothing wires it", "recommendation": "The plan's mid-build decision says recorded writer runs took 682-985 s, past the engine's 600 s default cell deadline, and that the kind sets its own deadline through writer_cell_timeout_s. The function (writer_kind.py:171-215) has no test. Nothing calls it: test_report_writer_exports.py lists it as awaiting its launcher, and report_writer_kind leaves cell_timeout_s unwired. Failure scenario: a host that wires report_writer_kind into a launch today, the public construction path, gets the 600 s default, and real-speed cells are cut off mid-report after they have been billed. The function's composition (writer turns plus judge phase, with the turn cap passed through) is also unverified. Add a test that pins its value against writer_ceiling_s plus judge_phase_ceiling_s. Either wire it where the kind is built or state in report_writer_kind's docstring that the caller must set the cell deadline from it. Scope: instance.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/ops/report_writer/writer_kind.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/actions/report_writing.py"], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "blocking", "title": "chunk-ref-missing unchecked: the plan's chunk headings do not parse, so no chunk deliverable was checked", "recommendation": "Manifest record_lint.unchecked: 'chunk-ref-missing unchecked \u2014 .prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-skills-under-test.md exposes no parseable chunk heading (`### Chunk NN: Name`), so no chunk section can be located and the deliverable check graded nothing.' cross-checks.md assigns this prefix BLOCKING, because a deliverable check that could not run is indistinguishable from one that passed. The plan's chunks are headed `### 01 \u2014 Skill seam: ...`, `### 02 \u2014 The report_writer candidate kind`, and so on. Rename every chunk heading to the parseable form (`### Chunk 01: Skill seam: a skill version is a value`, ...) and re-run critic-begin, so chunks 01 and 02's declared deliverables are graded. Scope: instance (one plan file, all six headings).", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-skills-under-test.md"], "fid": "R-5"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "warning", "title": "Writer kind copies the reporter kind's account/provider/candidate failure split, a third copy", "recommendation": "Scope: class. Each candidate kind hand-rolls the same mapping from a described failure's owner to a CandidateOutput: account means infra_errors plus account_refused=True, provider means infra_errors logged at WARNING, anything else means candidate_errors. ReportWriterKind._failed (writer_kind.py:474-514) copies analysis/reporter_kind.py:1147-1190 almost line for line, and run/judge_kind.py:1056-1073 is a third copy. Only the prefix text and the extra fields (telemetry, host_measures, kind_payload) differ. The routing is a rule the engine relies on: an account refusal has to stop the run. If a fourth owner value is added, or that rule changes, every copy must be edited by hand, and a copy that is missed sorts the cell into the wrong bucket without any error. Fix it by construction: add one kernel helper next to describe_failure/log_provider_failure in kernel/provider.py or kernel/candidate_kind.py. It would take the described failure, a label and the extra CandidateOutput fields and return the routed output. Then move all three kinds onto it. To bound the class, search for `account_refused=True` and `owner == \"provider\"` under packages/evals/src.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/ops/report_writer/writer_kind.py"], "fid": "R-6"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "warning", "title": "Bounce measures read the tally's JSON rollup by string key, so a renamed bounce kind becomes a zero", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. _measures (writer_kind.py:547-552) gets the validity and invariant counts from `tally.to_json()[\"total\"][\"bounce_kinds\"]`, an Any-typed serialization, using the bare strings \"validity\" and \"invariant\" with `.get(..., 0)`. Those strings are values of the producer's Literal in ops/report_writer/analyst.py:141, but Tally.record_bounce takes `kind: str`, so the type checker cannot connect the producer to this reader. If the analyst renames or splits a bounce kind, both measures quietly read 0.0, which reads as 'fewer bounces, better' in a corrected comparison and could promote the wrong arm. Fix: give Tally a typed accessor, for example `bounces(role) -> Counter[BounceKind]` with the analyst's Literal promoted to a named type used by both record_bounce and this reader, and read that instead of the JSON. The same accessor would make it a visible choice to leave out the other three kinds (unparsed, shape, max_tokens), which the plan's 'bounces by kind' covers and the kind does not measure today.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/ops/report_writer/writer_kind.py"], "fid": "R-7"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "warning", "title": "The revisions cap is a second private constant, and drift would make invoke raise", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. writer_contract.py:55 declares `_MOST_REVISIONS: Final = 2` 'as the writing loop holds it', duplicating loop.py's own private `_MOST_REVISIONS`, which WriterLimits.__post_init__ enforces. No test holds the two equal, unlike EffortWord, which test_the_effort_lever_names_the_words_the_model_client_takes pins. If someone lowers the loop's cap, WriterOverlays still validates the old range. invoke then builds `WriterLimits(revisions=self._overlays.revisions)` (writer_kind.py:396) outside any handler and raises ValueError, which breaks invoke's documented 'Never raises' and kills a run that has already spent. Fix: promote the loop's cap to a public name, since the contract is a production caller, and import it. Alternatively, validate the overlay by constructing WriterLimits. Either way there is one source of truth.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/ops/report_writer/writer_contract.py"], "fid": "R-8"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "Exports test docstring says report_writing 'exports nothing yet', but its __all__ holds campaign_report_writer", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. This changeset edited the paragraph in test_report_writer_exports.py:4-8, and it still says actions/report_writing.py 'exports nothing yet', while that module's __all__ is [\"campaign_report_writer\"] (report_writing.py:40). The parametrized assertions read __all__ directly, so the sentence is inert prose and no test reads it. Delete the claim rather than reword it.", "files": ["packages/evals/tests/test_report_writer_exports.py"], "fid": "R-9"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "warning", "title": "scope-trace: the report_writer kind has no launcher, and no chunk owns one, so its own cell deadline is never wired", "recommendation": "Instance. Nothing in src calls report_writer_kind (actions/report_writing.py:155), writer_cell_timeout_s (ops/report_writer/writer_kind.py:171), WRITER_KIND_CONTRACT or WRITER_KIND_MEASURES (writer_contract.py:109,163). The only callers are tests, and test_report_writer_exports.py lists them all as awaiting 'the writer kind's launcher'. Chunks 03-06 never name that launcher as a deliverable. The reporter kind's equivalent is ops/reporter.py. The plan's mid-build decision (build-plan line 46) says 'The kind sets its own deadline (writer_cell_timeout_s ...)', but the kind does not set it: a launcher has to pass it as KindWiring.cell_timeout_s. writer_cell_timeout_s also has no test. Consequence: chunk 06's paid Haiku smoke has no production path. If an ad-hoc launcher leaves out cell_timeout_s, cells fall back to the engine's 600 s default. The plan's own step-0 numbers (682-985 s) say that cuts a full report off, and those turns are paid for with no result. The delegated 03/04 builders each have reason to think someone else wires it. Fix: make the launcher (KindWiring with cell_timeout_s=writer_cell_timeout_s(...), and the kind's contract and measures on the profile) a named deliverable of a chunk before 06. Add a test that a launched writer cell gets the computed deadline, not the default. Or make the line-46 decision relational until that chunk lands.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/actions/report_writing.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/ops/report_writer/writer_kind.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/ops/report_writer/writer_contract.py"], "fid": "R-10"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "warning", "title": "Goals still marked inferred, one of them already built into the case shape", "recommendation": "Instance. The plan's '## Goals' keeps four items under 'Inferred (not owner words)': per-case withholding (line 28), the ~12-case dev/held-out split (line 26), gemini flash via OpenRouter as the fixed scoring judge, and regression as the same A/B. Chunk 05 adds a fifth inferred switch (line 91). Chunk 02 has already built per-case withholding into WriterCase.withhold (writer_kind.py:107), a shape frozen into every case's host_payload. If the owner disagrees, every case minted in chunk 04 has to be re-frozen. Get an owner ruling on at least the withholding item (and the judge model before 03 lands), or record why it stays inferred.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/ops/report_writer/writer_kind.py"], "fid": "R-11"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Mid-build decisions for the owner, and one alignment-pass miss", "recommendation": "Scope none. Decisions recorded and what settled each: (01) both roles' texts are built before the freeze, settled by the existing refusal order; write.py now calls load_skill/analyst(withhold) before the pricing check. (02 step 0) the writer gets its own deadline, settled by the recorded Opus runs at 682-985 s; still unwired, see the scope-trace finding. (02) the kind lives in ops/report_writer/ because analysis may not import ops. (02) an arm naming no skill records the shipped digest, not None; a departure from the brief, recorded as 